          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.089,
            0.639,
            0.112
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Fascinating Facts about Large Numbers"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.12,
            0.849,
            0.215
          ],
          "content": "Some interesting facts about large numbers are hidden below. Calculate the product or quotient to uncover the facts. Once you find the product or quotient, read the number in both Indian and American naming systems. Share your thoughts and questions about the fact with the class after you discover each number."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.404,
            0.253,
            0.499,
            0.271
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "1250 × 380"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.222,
            0.284,
            0.679,
            0.317
          ],
          "content": "is the number of kīrtanas composed by Purandaradāsa according to legends."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.222,
            0.316,
            0.678,
            0.381
          ],
          "content": "Purandaradāsa was a composer and singer in the 15th century. His kīrtanas spanned social reform, bhakti and spirituality. He systematised methods for teaching Carnatic music which is followed to the present day."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.687,
            0.232,
            0.852,
            0.42
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_15_image_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.198,
            0.47,
            0.418,
            0.623
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_15_image_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.427,
            0.511,
            0.763,
            0.559
          ],
          "content": "How many years did he live to compose so many songs? At what age did he start composing songs?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.427,
            0.558,
            0.743,
            0.605
          ],
          "content": "If he composed 4,75,000 songs, how many songs per year did he have to compose?"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.695,
            0.569,
            0.712
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "2100 × 70,000"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.277,
            0.725,
            0.531,
            0.742
          ],
          "content": "**is the approximate distance**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.276,
            0.74,
            0.572,
            0.772
          ],
          "continues_prev": true,
          "content": "**in kilometers, between the Earth and the Sun.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.277,
            0.771,
            0.741,
            0.804
          ],
          "content": "**This distance keeps varying throughout the year. The farthest distance is about 152 million kilometers.**"
        },
